            "notes": "The first few rounds are spent with typical tracer gameplay. Without high enough ability power or any CD reduction it isn't worth starting out with Flash Fist. The increased ammo and weapon power in the early rounds is enough to allow easier one clips for most DPS and supports. Pocket Bomb without too much initial AP investment still hits for roughly 120 damage and is a great way to finish off lower health targets, especially if combined with a melee prior to your recall which also makes the resulting pulse bomb easier to stick. An extra side effect of all the weaker pulse bombs being thrown around is that it eats up a lot of utility and survival cooldowns such as suzu. It isn't much but finding a way to weaponize your escapability can help draw the cooldowns out for the rest of your team.",
